\section{Numerical Modeling of Structure}
\label{sec:orgfa615c9}

The dynamics of the system is governed by the second-order differential equation:

\[ M\ddot{q} + C\dot{q} + Kq(t) = F^{\text{ext}}(t) \]

where:
\begin{description}
\item[{\(M\)}] Lumped Mass Matrix
\item[{\(C\)}] Damping Coefficient
\item[{\(K\)}] Spring Constant
\end{description}

and \(\ddot{q}(t)\), \(\dot{q}(t)\), \(q(t)\) represent acceleration, velocity, and position respectively.
\subsection{Magnetic Actuation}
\label{sec:org30cea04}

The magnetic force acting on the beam is given by:

\[F_{\text{magnetic}} = \chi B(t)^2 \cdot \mathbf{B}_{\text{direction}} \]

where:
\begin{description}
\item[{\(\chi\)}] Magnetic susceptibility of the material
\item[{\(B(t)\)}] Time-dependent magnetic field strength given by \(B(t) = B_{\text{strength}} \sin(2\pi f t)\), where \(f\) is the driving frequency
\item[{\(\mathbf{B}_{\text{direction}}\)}] Unit vector specifying the direction of the magnetic field
\end{description}
\subsection{Solution by Implicit Euler Method}
\label{sec:orga29a870}

The time integration is performed using the implicit Euler scheme:

\begin{align*}
q(t_{k+1}) &= q(t_k) + \dot{q}(t_{k+1}) \Delta t \\
\dot{q}(t_{k+1}) &= \dot{q}(t_k) + \ddot{q}(t_{k+1}) \Delta t
\end{align*}

where \(\Delta t\) is the timestep and subscripts \(k\) and \(k+1\) denote the current and next time levels respectively.
